ertilizers & Agrochemicals)"}],"target":{"ebitda_margin":20.1,"fy":"FY26","growth_basis":"7y CAGR","mcap":9438,"name":"SHARDA CROPCHEM LTD.","pat":681.0,"pat_growth":21.3,"pe":13.9,"rev":5267.6,"rev_growth":14.9,"s":"SHARDACROP"}},"plants":"","pre":0,"products":"{\"Agrochemicals\": [\"Fungicides\", \"Herbicides\", \"Insecticides\"]}","promises":[],"promises_total":0,"promoters":[{"name":"Mr Ramprakash V. Bubna","role":"Promoter, Chairman and Managing Director; husband of Mrs Sharda R. Bubna and father of Mr Ashish R. Bubna and Mr Manish R. Bubna"},{"name":"Mrs Sharda R. Bubna","role":"Promoter, Whole Time Director; wife of Mr Ramprakash V. Bubna and mother of Mr Ashish R. Bubna and Mr Manish R. Bubna"},{"name":"Mr Ashish R. Bubna","role":"Promoter, Whole Time Director; son of Mr Ramprakash V. Bubna and Mrs Sharda R. Bubna, brother of Mr Manish R. Bubna"},{"name":"Mr Manish R. Bubna","role":"Promoter, Whole Time Director; son of Mr Ramprakash V. Bubna and Mrs Sharda R. Bubna, brother of Mr Ashish R. Bubna"}],"related":"[{\"name\": \"Axis Crop Science Private Limited\", \"relation\": \"subsidiary\", \"note\": \"Indian subsidiary, 100% held; described in the related-party note as a wholly owned subsidiary (also referred to as Axis Cropscience Private Limited)\"}, {\"name\": \"Nihon Agro Service Kabushiki Kaisha\", \"relation\": …","risks":[{"note":"The entire model is registration-led, so delays in product registrations impede timely market entry; the BRSR flags this as the #1 material issue - timely regulatory approvals are critical for maintaining market access and introducing products across geographies, and delays or changing requirements may affect business continuity and growth plans, with negative implications for revenue realisation, compliance expenditure and access to target markets. Mitigation is to submit multiple registrations across regions to maintain regulatory readiness.","risk":"Delay in product registrations"},{"note":"Operating in a heavily regulated industry, the Company faces exposure to non-compliance leading to penalties or reputational harm, and regulatory frameworks governing crop protection products are becoming increasingly stringent. Mitigated by a compliance management system and a dedicated legal and regulatory team across key regions.","risk":"Regulatory and compliance risk"},{"note":"Oversupply or geopolitical disruptions may erode pricing power - a direct margin risk for a generic-portfolio distributor. Mitigation is operational efficiency, cost control and differentiated, value-added products.","risk":"Downward pricing pressure from oversupply and geopolitical disruption"},{"note":"Geopolitical tensions, trade restrictions, sanctions, shipping disruptions and volatility in global commodity and energy markets may impact sourcing, logistics, pricing and market access. The exposure is structural: the BRSR records exports at 100% of total turnover and Nil plants in India or internationally, so the Company depends entirely on third-party manufacturers and formulators and on cross-border trade. Mitigation is diversifying sourcing and supplier networks, strengthening inventory and supply chain planning, expanding geographic presence to reduce concentration risk, and monitoring trade policy.","risk":"Geopolitical and supply chain risk"},{"note":"Payment defaults or credit concerns among customers present risks to cash flows in a distribution model that carries receivables across many jurisdictions. Mitigated by customer due diligence, ongoing credit assessments and comprehensive global credit insurance coverage.","risk":"Customer credit risk"},{"note":"Currency fluctuations in cross-border transactions can impact financial performance. Mitigated by natural hedging that aligns US$ and EUR inflows with outflows, and by forward contracts.","risk":"Currency risk"},{"note":"Climate variability may disrupt agricultural cycles and business outcomes; changing weather patterns, water availability and evolving agricultural practices influence crop cycles, pest incidence and demand for crop protection products, creating demand volatility and market disruption in affected regions even as they open opportunities in climate-resilient products. Mitigated by broadening the product portfolio and geographic presence and investing in climate-resilient solutions.","risk":"Climate change and agricultural demand dynamics"},{"note":"The application of agrochemicals poses threats to human health and the surrounding environment, and any quality lapse could trigger product recalls, regulatory action and reputational impact. Mitigated by stringent biosafety protocols, compliance with environmental regulations, R&D investment in sustainable products, quality-assurance and supplier assessments, and periodic training for employees, distributors and farmers.","risk":"Biodiversity, environmental and product-stewardship risk"}],"rpt":{},"rpt_date":"","s":"SHARDACROP","sector":"Chemicals","sk":{"as_of":"2026-03-10","cagrs":[{"cagr":"~5%","period":"CY2025-CY2030","segment":"Global economy (nominal terms)"},{"cagr":"~6.5%","period":"through CY2030","segment":"India real GDP"}],"drivers":"Robust Indian crop production and rural demand supported by healthy reservoir levels and favourable monsoon|Government fiscal support to agriculture (rising Union Budget allocations)|High-value crop diversification (coconut, cashew, cocoa, sandalwood, agarwood, nuts) and orchard …","industry":"Fertilizers & Agrochemicals","market_size":[{"metric":"Union Budget 2026-27 allocation to agriculture sector","value":"Rs 1,62,671 crore (7% increase over revised FY2025-26 estimate of Rs 1,51,853 crore)","year":"FY2026-27"},{"metric":"India manufacturing sector target","value":"US$ 1 trillion","year":"FY2025-26"},{"metric":"India FDI inflow (cumulative)","value":"Over US$ 667.4 billion","year":"FY2014-FY2024"}],"overview":"The agrochemicals (crop protection) industry covers the development, manufacture and distribution of insecticides, herbicides, fungicides and plant growth regulators in Formulations and Technicals form. Per the issuer-commissioned ICRA Report (February 2026), the sector is supported by resilient Indian agriculture (healthy reservoir levels, robust crop production sustaining rural demand), a global 'China+1' shift favouring Indian chemical manufacturing, and sustained government fiscal support to agriculture and manufacturing.","peer_note":"drhp_issuer_selected — issue-driven, not exhaustive","peers":[],"schemes":"Make in India|Production Linked Incentive (PLI) scheme (incl. bulk drugs / KSM / API, total outlay Rs 6,940 crore FY2021-FY2030)|Bharat Vistar multilingual AI advisory platform (Union Budget)|Coconut Promotion Scheme and cashew-cocoa initiatives|PM Gati Shakti, National Logistics Policy, Dedicated …","structure":"The DRHP frames agrochemicals within globally dispersed supply chains for raw materials, intermediates and finished products, subject to tariff and trade-flow sensitivity. India is positioned as a beneficiary of 'China+1'/'Europe+1' localisation, with import substitution supported by PLI schemes …"},"strategies":"Keep investing in product registrations and identifying generic molecules approaching patent expiry - the registration portfolio is treated as the core competitive asset rather than plant capacity|Own registrations rather than manufacturing assets: retain the asset-light model so capital goes to registrations, intellectual property, market access, sourcing expertise and customer relationships|Advance the Factory-to-Farmer approach - move closer to end customers and deepen engagement across the agricultural value chain to improve responsiveness and market connection|Strengthen the distribution …","strengths":"Asset-light operating model - the BRSR reports Nil plants both nationally and internationally, so the business is run on registrations, sourcing relationships and distribution rather than owned manufacturing assets|Registration moat: 3,011 product registrations as on 31 March, 2026 plus a pipeline of 1,004 applications; management states 'the future of agrochemicals business lies in obtaining early product registrations due to the high entry barrier for new entrants'|Debt-free balance sheet, strong cash generation and disciplined capital allocation, which the Company says let it navigate …"},"meta":{"co":"SHARDA CROPCHEM LTD.","isin":"INE221J01015","s":"SHARDACROP","sector":"Chemicals"},"momentum":{"stock":{"mem":0,"s":"SHARDACROP","iid":"12829","c":"agg accumulation","g":3,"sig":"","d":51,"t":"","a":3.4,"lm":"2025-07","r":-30.3,"ft":"2025-07-29","m":7095,"cl":786.4,"ad":"2026-08-14","prev_stage":2,"prev_zone_vpe":null,"fam":"2025-07","pdd":"","atd":"2025-07-29","ins":{"has":true,"thesis":"Sharda Cropchem delivered record FY26 results with PAT doubling YoY to INR 681 Cr and EBITDA margins expanding 600 bps to 19.7%, driven by volume recovery and pricing power in Europe/LATAM. Management guides for sustained high margins  and 10-15% revenue growth in FY27, leveraging a moat of 3,011 product registrations despite geopolitical headwinds.","co":"SHARDA CROPCHEM LTD.","q":"Q4FY26","cd":"2026-05-19","sec":"Agrochemicals / Global Formulation & Registration Moat","layer":"Marketing, Distribution & Product Registration (Asset-Light)","cluster":"Pharma & Healthcare","trig":[],"st":[{"theme":"Chemicals & Fertilizers","subtheme":"Agrochemicals & crop-input cycle recovery","tag":"Agrochem","tier":"1","status":"Runner-up"}]},"sx":{"vpe_df_60d_sum":"-1.7","vpe_zone_cumul_df":"-1.5","pct_below_52w_high":"39.0","SMA_50":"873.9","duration_from_prev_signal":"","pct_change_from_prev_signal":"","drawdown_from_prev_signal":"","stage_changed_since_prev_signal":"","base_count":"","pivot_close":"","pivot_low":""}},"price":[["2022-12-30",514.95,1426381],["2023-01-02",503.25,330001],["2023-01-03",504.3,197453],["2023-01-04",488.8,241347],["2023-01-05",486.7,123656],["2023-01-06",493.05,331548],["2023-01-09",491.25,110750],["